  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Irudhaya Dinesh Kumar vs State Rep. By The on 29 October, 2025 Author: A.D.Jagadish Chandira Bench: A.D.Jagadish Chandira Crl.O In The High Court Of Judicature At Madras Dated : 29.10.2025 Coram: The Hon'Ble Mr. Justice A.D.Jagadish Chandira Crl.O.P.No. 29381 of 2025 Irudhaya Dinesh Kumar ... P Vs. State Rep. by the Inspector of Police, Mangalam Police Station, Tiruppur. ... R Prayer :",
    "facts": "This criminal original petition is filed to modify the condition imposed by the learned Judicial Magistrate IV, Tiruppur, dated 30.09.2025 in ECMP.No.2924 of 2025 in Crime No.146 of 2025.",
    "arguments": "2. The learned counsel for the petitioner would submit that the petitioner is an accused in Crime No.291 of 2025, registered by the respondent for the offences under Sections 123, 274 & 275 of BNS and 7(1) and 20 (2) of the Cigarettes and other Tobacco Products Act, 2003, and Section 59 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. It is his further contention that the petitioner's Maruthi Suzuki Ciaz Alpha car, bearing Registration No. TN 39 CC 5756, was also seized by the respondent. It is his further contention that the vehicle is of the year 2017 and the market value of the vehicle will not be more than Rs.2,00,000/-.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "2. The learned counsel for the petitioner would submit that the petitioner is an accused in Crime No.291 of 2025, registered by the respondent for the offences under Sections 123, 274 & 275 of BNS and 7(1) and 20 (2) of the Cigarettes and other Tobacco Products Act, 2003, and Section 59 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. It is his further contention that the petitioner's Maruthi Suzuki Ciaz Alpha car, bearing Registration No. TN 39 CC 5756, was also seized by the respondent. It is his further contention that the vehicle is of the year 2017 and the market value of the vehicle will not be more than Rs.2,00,000/-.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
